  "body": "Slice of #2007: the tool profile page only (parts C, D and E). The property grid (#2014) and the own modal (#2397) are not in this PR. FlamingFireCoding holds live claims on them.\n\n## What changed\n\n**C - one preview.** The Profile tab had a second side view of the tool, at a different scale. This PR removes it. The one to-scale preview beside the tool fields now draws the draft of the tab:\n- Draw holder, Custom: a holder outline that validates shows as the bands that the collision check sweeps (`tool_body::stack`, #2017).\n- Draw cutter: a cutter outline that validates replaces the steel outline. The holder goes on top of it as bands.\n- A draft that does not validate shows the holder in use. Its refusal stays in red under the table.\n- All other tabs show the holder in use, as before.\n\nThe new function `tool_profile_page::preview_inputs` is the one place that selects what the preview draws. `tool_preview::draw` takes an optional steel outline.\n\n**D - clipped rows.** I saw the cause in the running app before the change. Two causes:\n- egui gives a nested scroll area only the space that is left in the view (`egui-0.36.2/src/containers/scroll_area.rs`). When the table was low on the scrolled page, it fell to its 64 px least height and showed about two rows. The table now has a least height equal to its greatest height (150 px). A short table still shrinks to its rows.\n- The egui `Grid` has a 40 px least column width by default. The six columns were about 300 px wide in a 260 px column, so in a narrow pane the \"×\" buttons were outside the pane. The grid now has no least column width.\n- The tab row (Body, Profile, Draw holder, Draw cutter) and the three file buttons now wrap in a narrow column.\n\n**E - plain words, on this page only.**\n- \"landed: ...\" is now \"In use: ...\". Examples: \"In use: the holder cylinder from the dimensions\", \"In use: library holder BT30 ER20\", \"In use: a drawn cutter outline\".\n- The table headers are \"#\", \"height mm\", \"radius mm\" and \"arc\". Each header has a hover text.\n- The holder line reads \"holder Ø 44.0 × 35.0 mm, from 55.0 to 90.0 mm above the tip\".\n- The note reads \"The holder is a turned shape: you edit one half of its outline. Parts that are not round are covered by a larger safe shape, never cut away.\"\n- The hover texts of Parametric, Custom and Apply profile use plain words.\n\n`tool_settings.rs` has one edit of three lines: the preview call takes the output of `preview_inputs`. No other change goes into that file.\n\nEach edit still goes through the undoable commands that the page used before (Apply profile, Apply cutter). This PR adds no command.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2007-tool-profile-one-preview.md`.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nEmpty project, catalog tool EM-0600-4FL, Properties pane at 1600 x 1000.\n\nBefore - Profile tab, two previews, the table shows two rows:\n![before profile top](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/before-profile-top.png?raw=true)\n\nBefore - lower on the page:\n![before profile bottom](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/before-profile-bottom.png?raw=true)\n\nBefore - Draw cutter, the table shows rows 4 to 6 only:\n![before cutter](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/before-cutter.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter - Profile tab, one preview, all four rows:\n![after profile mid](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/after-profile-mid.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter - lower on the page, the file buttons wrap:\n![after profile bottom](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/after-profile-bottom.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter - Draw cutter, all six rows:\n![after cutter](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/screenshots/issue-2007/after-cutter.png?raw=true)\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `page_layout::layout_page_tool_profile` (new). It is the named layout test of the page. In a narrow pane, the tab row, each \"×\" and the file buttons stay in the leaf. In the default window, the line under the table starts below the last row. I removed each part of the fix one at a time, and the test failed each time:\n  - without the least height: \"the table hides rows - its last row ends at 1233.5, the line under it starts at 1203\";\n  - without the column-width change: \"\\\"×\\\" ... leaves the leaf\".\n- `tool_profile::tool_profile_structure` (new, the structural twin of the page). It checks the order of the rows in the third column, the table headers, and that no label contains \"landed\". The test is in `tool_profile.rs` because `structural.rs` is already longer than 400 lines.\n- `tool_one_preview::the_profile_tab_draws_its_drafts_in_the_one_preview` (new). There is one preview and no side view on Draw holder and on Draw cutter. A Custom holder at r 40 reaches r 40 in the preview bands. A drawn cutter gives a steel outline.\n- Updated assertions: `tool_profile::profile_tab_states_conservative_envelope_and_half_profile_rules_and_dxf_workflow` and `tool_holder_reference.rs` (the new \"In use\" text).\n\nResults on head `aa75d2a34`:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green, 9 steps, 0 failed (ui lib 153 s, and the ui suites boundary, boundary_picks, sinker_setup, tap_hand, theme_example, theme_files and waterjet_tool).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The `#[test]` count of `crates/ui` goes up by 3. No test is deleted or ignored. No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The pixel snapshots (release lane).\n- A long imported DXF or STEP outline in the app. A table with more rows than 150 px scrolls inside its area, as before.\n- Inch units in the app. The headers use `u.suffix()`, as before.\n- Frame cost: on the Profile tab with Custom, the holder draft is validated two times each frame (once for the preview, once for the section). This was already so for the body envelope. It is not measured here.\n- A turning tool. Its page has no Profile tab and has no change.\n\nChangelog: Tool editor, Profile tab: one to-scale preview draws the drawn holder or cutter, the points table shows all its rows, and the page uses plain words (\"In use\", \"height\", \"radius\").\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #2007\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
